# Repository-wide git attributes.
#
# The point of this file is honesty about provenance: GitHub's language bar, its
# diffs and its "generated" badge are how a reader decides what in here is
# *ours*. Without these lines the vendored ArtCraft Launcher snapshot (ADR-0015)
# is credited to this project — 100% of the Rust, Shell, PowerShell and Nix in
# this repository lives under packages/craft-launcher and none of it was written
# here. See docs/THIRD_PARTY_POLICY.md rule T-5.
#
# Deliberately absent: global `text eol=lf` rules. Line-ending normalisation
# rewrites bytes on checkout, and a vendored snapshot must stay byte-identical
# to upstream or the trademark permission covering it lapses. `-text` below
# guarantees git never touches those files.

# --- Vendored third-party snapshot ------------------------------------------
# linguist-vendored : excluded from GitHub's language statistics and collapsed
#                     by default in pull-request diffs. It stays in the checkout
#                     and still builds — this only changes how GitHub describes it.
# -text             : no EOL conversion ever, so what upstream published is what
#                     lands on disk. Verified byte-for-byte against the pinned
#                     commit by tests/test_vendored_integrity.py.
packages/craft-launcher/** linguist-vendored -text

# --- Machine-generated files -------------------------------------------------
# Not hand-written source; marked so review attention goes where it belongs.
packages/craft-launcher/Cargo.lock linguist-generated -text
packages/web/package-lock.json linguist-generated

# --- Binary assets -----------------------------------------------------------
# Every binary in this repository currently lives under the vendored tree.
# `binary` is the -diff -merge -text macro: no textual diffs and no EOL
# normalisation. Normalising line endings inside an .icns or .png would corrupt
# the file — and would also break the integrity manifest in docs/vendored/.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.tiff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
